**Week 12: Documentation and Best Practices**

**Create Integration Testing Best Practices Guide**:

File: `docs/integration-testing-best-practices.md`

```markdown
# Integration Testing Best Practices with Testcontainers

## Container Configuration

### Use Specific Image Tags
❌ Bad: `new PostgreSQLContainer<>("postgres")`  // Uses 'latest', unstable
✓ Good: `new PostgreSQLContainer<>("postgres:14.2")`  // Specific version, reproducible

### Configure Wait Strategies
```java
@Container
static PostgreSQLContainer<?> postgres = new PostgreSQLContainer<>("postgres:14.2")
    .waitingFor(Wait.forLogMessage(".*database system is ready.*", 2))
    .withStartupTimeout(Duration.ofMinutes(2));
```text

### Use Container Reuse for Performance
```java
@Container
static PostgreSQLContainer<?> postgres = new PostgreSQLContainer<>("postgres:14.2")
    .withReuse(true);  // Reuse across test classes
```text

## Test Data Management

### Use Test Data Builders
```java
Member member = aMember()
    .withName("Jane", "Doe")
    .active()
    .buildAndSave(repository);
```text

### Clean Up State Between Tests
```java
@AfterEach
void cleanup() {
    memberRepository.deleteAll();  // Clean database state
    redisTemplate.getConnectionFactory().getConnection().flushAll();  // Clear Redis
}
```text

### Use Transactions for Rollback
```java
@Test
@Transactional  // Automatically rolls back after test
void shouldTestWithAutoRollback() {
    // Test code
}
```text

## Performance Optimization

### Parallel Test Execution
```xml
<plugin>
    <groupId>org.apache.maven.plugins</groupId>
    <artifactId>maven-surefire-plugin</artifactId>
    <configuration>
        <parallel>classes</parallel>
        <threadCount>4</threadCount>
    </configuration>
</plugin>
```text

### Container Reuse
Enable in `~/.testcontainers.properties`:
```properties
testcontainers.reuse.enable=true
```text

### Docker Image Caching
- CI/CD: Cache Docker images between pipeline runs
- Local: Docker automatically caches pulled images

## Common Pitfalls

### Pitfall 1: Not Waiting for Async Operations
❌ Bad:
```java
kafkaTemplate.send("topic", message);
assertNotNull(repository.findById(id));  // May fail, consumer not processed yet
```text

✓ Good:
```java
kafkaTemplate.send("topic", message);
await().atMost(10, TimeUnit.SECONDS).untilAsserted(() -> {
    assertNotNull(repository.findById(id));
});
```text

### Pitfall 2: Hardcoding Ports
❌ Bad:
```java
String url = "jdbc:postgresql://localhost:5432/test";  // Fixed port, conflicts
```text

✓ Good:
```java
@DynamicPropertySource
static void props(DynamicPropertyRegistry registry) {
    registry.add("spring.datasource.url", postgres::getJdbcUrl);  // Dynamic port
}
```text

### Pitfall 3: Not Cleaning Up Test Data
❌ Bad: Test data pollutes database, next test fails

✓ Good: Use `@AfterEach` cleanup or `@Transactional` rollback
```

