### Example 1: Member Service Database Integration Test (Michigan Incident Prevention)

**Scenario**: Database Connection Pool Exhaustion Not Detected by Unit Tests

**Problem**:
- **Unit Tests**: Mocked `MemberRepository` always succeeded; no real database connection pool testing
- **Production**: PostgreSQL connection pool configured with 20 connections; Member Service under load exhausted pool
- **Impact**: 2,400 member portal users unable to log in; 4-hour outage; $95K operational cost

**Without Integration Tests** (What Happened):

Unit test with mock (passes, but doesn't catch connection pool issue):

```java
@ExtendWith(MockitoExtension.class)
class MemberServiceUnitTest {
    @Mock
    private MemberRepository repository;

    @InjectMocks
    private MemberService service;

    @Test
    void shouldCreateMember() {
        Member member = new Member("M12345", "John", "Doe");
        when(repository.save(any())).thenReturn(member);

        Member created = service.createMember("M12345", "John", "Doe");

        assertEquals("M12345", created.getMemberId());
        // TEST PASSES ✓
        // But doesn't test real database connection pool behavior
    }
}
```

**Production deployment**: Connection pool exhaustion under load → 4-hour outage → $95K cost

**With Testcontainers Integration Test** (Prevents Production Incident):

```java
@SpringBootTest
@Testcontainers
class MemberServiceConnectionPoolIntegrationTest {

    @Container
    static PostgreSQLContainer<?> postgres = new PostgreSQLContainer<>("postgres:14.2")
        .withDatabaseName("members")
        .withInitScript("db/schema.sql");

    @DynamicPropertySource
    static void postgresProps(DynamicPropertyRegistry registry) {
        registry.add("spring.datasource.url", postgres::getJdbcUrl);
        registry.add("spring.datasource.hikari.maximum-pool-size", () -> 20);  // Match production config
    }

    @Autowired
    private MemberService memberService;

    @Test
    void shouldHandleHighConcurrencyWithConnectionPool() {
        // Simulate 50 concurrent requests (production load test)
        ExecutorService executor = Executors.newFixedThreadPool(50);
        CountDownLatch latch = new CountDownLatch(50);
        AtomicInteger successCount = new AtomicInteger(0);
        AtomicInteger failureCount = new AtomicInteger(0);

        for (int i = 0; i < 50; i++) {
            final int id = i;
            executor.submit(() -> {
                try {
                    memberService.createMember("M" + id, "First" + id, "Last" + id);
                    successCount.incrementAndGet();
                } catch (Exception e) {
                    failureCount.incrementAndGet();
                    System.err.println("Connection pool exhausted: " + e.getMessage());
                } finally {
                    latch.countDown();
                }
            });
        }

        // Wait for all requests to complete
        assertTrue(latch.await(60, TimeUnit.SECONDS));

        // Assert: All requests should succeed with properly configured pool
        assertEquals(50, successCount.get(), "Expected all requests to succeed");
        assertEquals(0, failureCount.get(), "Expected no connection pool failures");

        // TEST WOULD FAIL if pool configured with only 20 connections for 50 concurrent requests
        // Forces developer to increase pool size or add connection timeout handling
    }
}
```

**Result**:
- **Integration Test Detects Issue**: Test fails with connection pool exhaustion error
- **Developer Action**: Increases connection pool size from 20 → 100 connections
- **Production Deployment**: No connection pool exhaustion; handles load successfully
- **Incident Prevention ROI**: **$95K cost avoidance**

