### Example 3: Provider API External Timeout Handling (Ohio Incident Prevention)

**Scenario**: External State API Timeout Handling Not Tested

**Problem**:
- **Unit Tests**: Mocked external API always responded instantly; no timeout testing
- **Production**: State licensing API has 5% timeout rate; Provider Service inadequate timeout handling
- **Impact**: 120K provider queries failed; 8-hour outage; $180K SLA penalty

**Without Integration Tests** (What Happened):

Unit test with mock (passes, but doesn't test timeouts):

```java
@ExtendWith(MockitoExtension.class)
class ProviderServiceUnitTest {
    @Mock
    private StateLicensingClient externalClient;

    @InjectMocks
    private ProviderService service;

    @Test
    void shouldVerifyProviderLicense() {
        LicenseResponse mockResponse = new LicenseResponse("MD-12345", "ACTIVE");
        when(externalClient.checkLicense("MD-12345")).thenReturn(mockResponse);

        ProviderLicenseStatus status = service.verifyProviderLicense("MD-12345");

        assertEquals("ACTIVE", status.getStatus());
        // TEST PASSES ✓
        // But doesn't test timeout handling (mock responds instantly)
    }
}
```

**Production**: State API timeouts → Provider Service crashes → 8-hour outage → $180K penalty

**With Testcontainers Integration Test** (Prevents Production Incident):

```java
@SpringBootTest
@Testcontainers
class ProviderExternalAPITimeoutIntegrationTest {

    @Container
    static GenericContainer<?> wiremock = new GenericContainer<>("wiremock/wiremock:2.35.0")
        .withExposedPorts(8080);

    @DynamicPropertySource
    static void wiremockProps(DynamicPropertyRegistry registry) {
        String url = "http://" + wiremock.getHost() + ":" + wiremock.getFirstMappedPort();
        registry.add("external.licensing.api.url", () -> url);
        registry.add("external.licensing.api.timeout", () -> 5000);  // 5-second timeout
    }

    @Autowired
    private ProviderService providerService;

    private WireMock wireMockClient;

    @BeforeEach
    void setupWireMock() {
        wireMockClient = new WireMock(wiremock.getHost(), wiremock.getFirstMappedPort());
    }

    @Test
    void shouldHandleExternalAPITimeout() {
        // Configure WireMock to simulate 10-second delay (exceeds 5-second timeout)
        wireMockClient.register(get(urlPathEqualTo("/api/licenses/MD-12345"))
            .willReturn(aResponse()
                .withStatus(200)
                .withFixedDelay(10000)  // 10-second delay
                .withBody("{\"licenseNumber\":\"MD-12345\",\"status\":\"ACTIVE\"}")
            )
        );

        // Act & Assert: Service should handle timeout gracefully
        ProviderLicenseTimeoutException exception = assertThrows(
            ProviderLicenseTimeoutException.class,
            () -> providerService.verifyProviderLicense("MD-12345")
        );

        // Verify exception message provides actionable information
        assertTrue(exception.getMessage().contains("timeout after 5000ms"));

        // Verify retry logic NOT executed for timeout (fail fast)
        wireMockClient.verifyThat(1, getRequestedFor(urlPathEqualTo("/api/licenses/MD-12345")));

        // TEST WOULD FAIL if timeout handling missing or inadequate
        // Forces developer to implement proper timeout handling
    }

    @Test
    void shouldRetryOnTransientErrors() {
        // First 2 attempts return 503 Service Unavailable, 3rd succeeds
        wireMockClient.register(get(urlPathEqualTo("/api/licenses/MD-12345"))
            .inScenario("Retry")
            .whenScenarioStateIs(STARTED)
            .willReturn(aResponse().withStatus(503).withFixedDelay(100))
            .willSetStateTo("First Retry")
        );

        wireMockClient.register(get(urlPathEqualTo("/api/licenses/MD-12345"))
            .inScenario("Retry")
            .whenScenarioStateIs("First Retry")
            .willReturn(aResponse().withStatus(503).withFixedDelay(100))
            .willSetStateTo("Second Retry")
        );

        wireMockClient.register(get(urlPathEqualTo("/api/licenses/MD-12345"))
            .inScenario("Retry")
            .whenScenarioStateIs("Second Retry")
            .willReturn(aResponse()
                .withStatus(200)
                .withBody("{\"licenseNumber\":\"MD-12345\",\"status\":\"ACTIVE\"}")
            )
        );

        // Should eventually succeed after retries
        ProviderLicenseStatus status = providerService.verifyProviderLicense("MD-12345");
        assertEquals("ACTIVE", status.getStatus());

        // Verify retry logic executed (3 total requests)
        wireMockClient.verifyThat(3, getRequestedFor(urlPathEqualTo("/api/licenses/MD-12345")));
    }
}
```

**Result**:
- **Integration Test Detects Missing Timeout Handling**: Test fails; timeout exception not handled
- **Developer Action**: Implements timeout handling with circuit breaker, retry logic
- **Production Deployment**: State API timeouts handled gracefully; no outage
- **Incident Prevention ROI**: **$180K cost avoidance**

